{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>יעשוק נהר</b> — It is so enormous: when it drinks the river's waters, it will appear that the waters are lacking; therefore he used the word יעשוק [oppresses/drains]." "<b>ולא יחפוז</b> — It will not drink hastily, for it does not fear beast or man, and so it trusts." "<b>כי יגיח</b> — Like מגיח ממקומו [surging from its place]. And the meaning is close to 'going forth.' Similarly: אתה גוחי מבטן."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:05:31.160801024Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}